    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d932">

                <pb facs="1035" n="1025" xml:id="pg1025"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">340.1115A/11–744: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Kennan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-11-07T12:00:00+03:00">November 7,
                            1944—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 12:35 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4260. ReDepts 2610, November 4, 8 p.m.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d932-f1"/> We have
                    inquired through the Foreign Office whether the Soviet postal authorities are
                    agreeable to the resumption of parcel post service from the U. S. to the Soviet
                    Union. We will endeavor to obtain an early reply but a delay of several weeks is
                    possible.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kennan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d932-f1" n="2" xml:id="d932-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; this telegram indicated that the Post Office Department proposed to
                    resume parcel post service immediately with all of the Soviet Union
                    (340.1115a/10–2844).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
